0..75 Comment "// The one-time pad of `std.crypto` hides its message: under a uniform key,"
76..127 Comment "// the ciphertext is uniform, whatever the message."
128..130 Comment "//"
131..206 Comment "// Perfect secrecy is the independence of the ciphertext and the message. A"
207..281 Comment "// key is a fresh draw, so this is the reading of a fresh name as a random"
282..349 Comment "// draw. A key used twice leaks the difference of its two messages."
350..352 Comment "//"
353..431 Comment "// At `w = 2`, each of the messages 1 and 2 gives a uniform ciphertext under a"
432..505 Comment "// key of 2 bits. `joint` draws the message as well, and states the joint"
506..584 Comment "// distribution of the message and the ciphertext. Each of its 8 pairs has the"
585..661 Comment "// weight `1/8`. `reused` pads two messages with one key, and the difference"
662..740 Comment "// of the two ciphertexts reveals the message. A crate test reads both joints,"
741..779 Comment "// and `independent` decides each one."
780..782 Comment "//"
783..847 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/crypto.gandr` — the pad and the key"
848..921 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/corpus.rs` — the decision of"
922..939 Comment "//   independence"
940..955 Comment "// - see: #5713"
957..993 Comment "// The host interface of randomness."
